card.statement:
Suppose $\phi\not\in\Z.\1$ or, equivalently, $\comp(\phi)=\emptyset$.

- By Proposition <<ref:objets-de-niveau-0>>, $P_\phi$ is a simple $\B_1^{\bar{q},\Lambda}$-weight module. Its corresponding scheme is as follows:

\[
\xymatrix@!C{
\dots
& \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1}
& \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1} \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1}
& \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1} \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1}
& v_{\alpha-1}  \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1} \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1}
& v_\alpha      \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1} \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1}
& v_{\alpha+1}  \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1} \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1}
& v_{\alpha+2}  \ar@(ul,ur)^{z_1} \ar@/^/[r]^{x_1} \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1}
&                                    \ar@/^/[l]^{y_1} & \dots\\
}
\]

where we have added in the scheme the action of $z_1$ for the sake of completeness.

- By Proposition <<ref:iso-des-P-phi>>, for all $\Psi\in\Z.\phi$, $P_\phi$ and $P_\Psi$ are isomorphic in
$\B_1^{\bar{q},\Lambda}-\wMod$.
